import pathlib,json,html,base64,io,hashlib,time
from PIL import Image
P=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
R=json.loads((P/'results.json').read_text());D=json.loads((P/'decisions.json').read_text());G={g['group']:g for g in json.loads((P/'groups.json').read_text())};prompts={p['id']:p['prompt'] for p in json.loads((P/'prompts.json').read_text())}
def esc(x):return html.escape(str(x))
parts=['<!doctype html><html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>CONSENSUS-007 — private pilot</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:35px auto;padding:15px;color:#182536}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{padding:9px;border:1px solid #cad4df}img{width:23%;margin:0.5%}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#f0f4f8;padding:16px}h1,h2{color:#183c64}.note{background:#fff0ca;padding:18px}</style><h1>Can four anonymous images reveal one substitute?</h1><p class="note">CONSENSUS-007 · Private exploratory research · Scientific review pending</p><p>One RTX3090 simulates four orchestrators. Forty new benign prompt families, 20 honest calibration groups and 20 heldout prompts; four independently seeded SD1.4 images, one SD1.5 and one SDXL image per prompt. No reference model or model label enters a decision. This measures relative consistency, not promised model identity, execution proof or dishonest behavior.</p><h2>Heldout decisions</h2><table><tr><th>Embedding / group</th><th>Valid / scheduled</th><th>Correct substitute</th><th>Wrong honest slot</th><th>False accusations</th><th>No clear outlier</th><th>Rank correct</th></tr>']
for method,conds in R['heldout'].items():
 for cond,r in conds.items():parts.append('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(x)+'</td>' for x in [method+' / '+cond,f"{r['valid']} / {r['scheduled']}",r['correct'],r['wrong_honest_slot'],r['false_accusation'],r['abstention'],f"{r['rank_correct']}/{r['rank_denominator']}" if r['rank_denominator'] is not None else '—'])+'</tr>')
parts.append('</table><p>Rank-only choices have a 25% random-choice context; they are not detection rates. Conditions reuse honest images and prompts, so they are paired, not independent samples. Invalid groups are excluded from valid denominators and retained in JSON; they are not scored as ordinary abstentions.</p><h2>Frozen method and uncertainty</h2><p>For each image, score = minimum cosine distance to any peer divided by the median pairwise distance within the remaining trio, floored at 1e−12. Only a unique highest score strictly above its threshold flags a slot; ties abstain. Each embedding threshold is the maximum of 20 all-honest calibration maxima, nominal 1/21 ≈ 5% under exchangeability, not validated production false-alarm control. No substitute labels or heldout outcomes set thresholds. Thresholds and blind decisions were written before evaluation labels were opened. No combined OR rule.</p><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(R['thresholds'],indent=2))+'</pre><p>RPA is the frozen FORENSIC-006 1024-dimensional mean embedding over 64 nonoverlapping patches. PickScore uses only its frozen image encoder, no prompt/text features. RGB512 inputs only. SDXL generated natively at1024 then resized, a configuration/resolution confound; SD1x generated512. DDIM25, guidance7.5, float16 CPU-generated independent latents, empty negative prompt. Existing SD1x safety checkers retained; base SDXL has no built-in checker and its watermark is disabled as in precedent. Zero rerolls, training, downloads or hosted inference.</p><h2>Descriptive 95% Wilson intervals</h2><pre>')
parts.append(esc(json.dumps({m:{c:{k:v for k,v in r.items() if k.startswith('wilson')} for c,r in cs.items()} for m,cs in R['heldout'].items()},indent=2))+'</pre><p>Only20 heldout prompt families. These intervals describe this small pilot; they do not certify deployment performance or address distribution shift. JPEG75 changes one honest image only with the original preserved and unchanged thresholds.</p><h2>Repeated-job exploration</h2><p>Four disjoint five-prompt heldout blocks keep operator roles fixed and shuffle submission order per job. Arithmetic mean per-role score is ranked, with no detection threshold. Four blocks cannot calibrate a5% alarm. Honest block ranges are retained below.</p><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(R['repeated_job_rank_only'],indent=2))+'</pre>')
selected=[]
def add(g):
 if g not in selected:selected.append(g)
for cond in ['honest','close','broad']:add(next(r['group'] for r in D if r['split']=='heldout' and r['condition']==cond))
for method in ['rpa','pickscore']:
 for cond in ['close','broad']:
  for correct in [True,False]:
   candidates=[r for r in D if r['method']==method and r['split']=='heldout' and r['condition']==cond and r['valid'] and (r['outcome']=='correct')==correct]
   if candidates:add(candidates[0]['group'])
parts.append('<h2>Deterministically selected real groups</h2><p>First heldout honest/close/broad, then first detected and first missed substitute for each method/condition where present; deduplicated, no visual selection. Labels shown only after blind decisions.</p>');(P/'examples').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for gid in selected:
 g=G[gid];parts.append('<h3>'+esc(gid+' / '+g['condition']+' / '+prompts[g['prompt_id']])+'</h3>')
 for slot,key in enumerate(g['members']):
  path=P/'normalized'/(key+'.png')
  if not path.exists():parts.append('<span>Missing '+esc(key)+'</span>');continue
  im=Image.open(path).convert('RGB');im.thumbnail((210,210));b=io.BytesIO();im.save(b,format='JPEG',quality=80);(P/'examples'/(gid+'-'+str(slot)+'.jpg')).write_bytes(b.getvalue());parts.append('<img alt="slot '+str(slot)+'" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,'+base64.b64encode(b.getvalue()).decode()+'">')
 parts.append('<pre>'+esc(json.dumps([dict(method=r['method'],decision=r['decision'],truth=r['truth'],outcome=r['outcome'],scores=r.get('scores')) for r in D if r['group']==gid],indent=2))+'</pre>')
parts.append('<h2>Accounting, verification and reproduction</h2><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(R['accounting'],indent=2))+'</pre><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(R['verification'],indent=2))+'</pre><p>Use existing Smart NV environment only; no installation required. Full raw/normalized images remain in '+esc(str(P))+' remotely. Inspect any group by mapping groups.json members to normalized/&lt;anonymous-id&gt;.png; generation labels are in separate labels.json and schedule.json. Compact local bundle includes selected thumbnails, all features, distances and decisions, manifests, scripts and hashes, excluding models, environment and credentials.</p><pre>cd '+esc(str(P))+'\nPY=/home/smart/repos/livepeer/research/judge-score-fingerprinting-poc/2026-10-25/.venv/bin/python\n# Frozen source hashes: freeze.json. Completed results: results.json.\n# Run peer synthetic checks: $PY peer.py\n# Verify snapshot: sha256sum -c snapshot.sha256\n# Generation is non-rerunnable in place: create a fresh directory for a fresh run.\n# Original execution: generate.py sd14; generate.py sd15; generate.py sdxl; extract.py; analyze.py; report.py\n# analyze.py refuses an existing thresholds.json; preserve threshold and decision records.</pre><p>Recommendation: assess each representation by correct flags, wrong accusations, abstentions and JPEG nuisance behavior together. A peer-consistency flag alone is insufficient evidence of model identity or misconduct. This bounded pilot provides evidence about this particular stochastic image setup; scientific review is pending.</p></html>')
(P/'report.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
